Determine the historical development of squash from the older game of rackets and its evolution into the modern sport.
Squash originated from the older game of rackets in the early 19th century. The sport of rackets, which was played with wooden rackets and a ball, was popular in England, particularly among prisoners in London's King's Bench and Fleet debtors prisons in the 18th century. It evolved from the game of fives, where players used tennis rackets to increase the speed of play and hit the ball against walls.

In 1830, during the time when rackets were still being played, squash was invented at Harrow School as a variation of the game. The new sport, squash, introduced several changes, including the use of a smaller, harder ball and a more enclosed court, which allowed for faster-paced gameplay. Over time, squash developed into its own distinct sport, separate from rackets, and eventually gained international popularity. While both sports share some similarities, such as the use of stringed rackets, squash has evolved significantly in terms of rules, equipment, and playing style, becoming a modern indoor racket sport played globally.
