Operation Noah (charity) was founded in 2004 by Christian Ecology Link (CEL) and officially launched in October of that year. It later became a joint project of CEL and the Environmental Issues Network of Churches Together in Britain and Ireland.

**Primary Objectives:**  
The primary objective of Operation Noah is to campaign exclusively on climate change as an ecumenical Christian charity based in the UK. It focuses on raising awareness, advocating for action, and promoting solutions to address climate change through a cross-denominational approach.
