The composer of "Fantasia on a Theme by Thomas Tallis" is Ralph Vaughan Williams. The work was composed in 1910 and first performed on 10 September 1910 at Gloucester Cathedral during the Three Choirs Festival. Vaughan Williams conducted the premiere, which was a significant success. He later revised the piece in 1913 and 1919. The composition is based on a melody from Thomas Tallis's "Third Mode Melody," which inspired Vaughan Williams to create this work.
