The co-founders of Apple Computers, along with Steve Jobs, were Steve Wozniak and Ronald Wayne. The company was founded on April 1, 1976. Steve Wozniak designed and hand-built the company's first product, the Apple I, while Steve Jobs focused on business development and marketing. Ronald Wayne provided administrative oversight for the new venture. However, Wayne soon sold his share of the company back to Jobs and Wozniak for $800, and later accepted $1,500 to forfeit any claims against Apple.
