Additionally, the French word "trident" refers to a three-pronged spear used for spear fishing and historically as a polearm. It is associated with Poseidon (Neptune) in Greek mythology and Shiva in Hindu mythology as the "trishula." The word "trident" originates from Latin "tridens" or "tridentis," meaning "three-toothed" or "three-pronged."

These weapons—javelin and trident—are named after French words and have distinct designs, usages, and cultural significances.
