Describe the key services and technologies typically associated with ISPs, such as broadband, DNS, and IP address allocation.
Internet service providers (ISPs) typically offer a range of services and technologies, including broadband Internet access, domain name registration (DNS), and IP address allocation. Broadband allows for high-speed Internet connectivity, enabling users to access the Internet efficiently. DNS services translate human-readable domain names into IP addresses that computers use to identify each other on the network. IP address allocation involves assigning unique IP addresses to devices connected to the Internet, often using DHCP to manage a pool of available addresses dynamically. These services are essential for enabling seamless Internet communication and access.
