Identify the artistic movement and style associated with the works of Monet and Renoir, including key characteristics and historical context.
The artistic movement and style associated with the works of Monet and Renoir is Impressionism. Key characteristics of Impressionism include the pioneering use of light in painting, as the artists attempted to capture light as seen from the human eye. This movement emerged from the naturalist ethic of Realism and was influenced by the desire to depict contemporary life and scenes. Notable figures in this movement include Édouard Manet, Claude Monet, Camille Pissarro, and Pierre-Auguste Renoir. The historical context of Impressionism includes its development in France during the 19th century, following the desecration of Notre Dame de Paris Cathedral during the French Revolution, which led to a renewed interest in Gothic architecture and artistic innovation.
