The poem "Samson Agonistes" is authored by John Milton. It is a tragic closet drama, which means it was intended for reading rather than performance. This work was published in 1671 as part of the volume that also included "Paradise Regained." Milton began working on "Samson Agonistes" around the same time as "Paradise Regained," but it was completed after the larger work. The poem is part of Milton's body of work that includes his epic poems such as "Paradise Lost" and reflects his engagement with themes of heroism, faith, and tragedy. "Samson Agonistes" is considered to be within the literary movement of English Renaissance poetry, characterized by its use of classical forms and themes, as well as its exploration of human struggle and divine will.
