Identify the sport that features a hog line and explain its definition, purpose, and how it functions within the sport's rules and gameplay.
The sport that features a hog line is curling. The hog line is a boundary line on the curling sheet, specifically the near hog line, which marks the point from which a stone must be released. If a stone's front edge crosses the near hog line before it is released, it is considered a violation. The hog line serves to ensure fair play by enforcing rules regarding the release of stones. Sweepers use the hog line to gauge the weight and speed of a stone, as the time it takes for a stone to travel from the hog line to the tee line can indicate its potential stopping point. In major tournaments, an electronic sensor called the "eye on the hog" is used to detect hog line violations, ensuring strict enforcement of the rules.
