Identify the historical medical uses and common names for tincture of opium in medicinal practice
Based on the provided context, tincture of opium, historically known as laudanum, had various medical uses and common names in medicinal practice. Its historical medical uses included treating pain, cough suppression, and severe diarrhea. Common names for tincture of opium include laudanum, Paracelsus' laudanum, Sydenham's Laudanum (also known as "tinctura opii crocata"), benzoic laudanum ("tinctura opii benzoica"), and deodorized tincture of opium. Additionally, it is referred to as Paregoric or camphorated tincture of opium ("tinctura opii camphorata").
